          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: फ़ुरसत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फ़ुरसत — fursat — \"free time; leisure\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फ़ुरसत (fursat) में मैं कहानियाँ पढ़ता हूँ। Fursat meṁ maiṁ kahāniyā̃ paṛhtā hūṁ. In my free time I read stories."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फ़ुरसत (fursat) is usually traced to Arabic furṣa, \"an occasion, a chance\", which reached Hindi through Persian; in Hindi it is time with nothing that must be done."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
